  "readme": "# Scout selection diagnostics ordinary full16\n\nThe fresh K run passed all 16 ordinary two-client lifecycle checks: realm 1792977848891-7c9f3b5a, protocol run 1792977859487-2ff0ea0f, with **343 ordinary sent commands**. The first shared-drop attempt produced no loot and remains recorded as failed; the second attempt passed. Prior J349 and older351/341 command runs remain separate.\n\nBackend build c743122af05faca43d9535d8c6c2a4bfb01b924f, its 50 inputs/09081 aggregate and immutable dae1 Release are reused. Current driver and execution commit are b5374083d257d375437af3de42bead159cd2b917. The six ordinary drivers and 16 assertions are separate from the nine-input Node232 regression. No Rust rebuild or new backend Release is claimed.\n\nNormal exit was0; all six counters were zero before and after. Root independently observed PID59644 absent and ports17600/17610 free. The ordinary run retains its 900-second total limit. This archive does not independently replay a per-request900ms attack deadline, certify capacity, establish a formal25 improvement, or establish GUI/P0/P2 acceptance. The existing audit checked13 public files and six private values for credential absence; no private values are copied.\n\n- [Report](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f.report.json), [owned realm](public/1792977848891-7c9f3b5a.realm-evidence.json), [independent audit](public/1792977848891-7c9f3b5a.independent-audit.json), [source proof](public/1792977848891-7c9f3b5a.source-manifest-verification.json), [Zone metrics](public/1792977848891-7c9f3b5a.zone-metrics.json).\n- [Paired trace A](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-a.trace.jsonl), [paired trace B](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-b.trace.jsonl), [relogin0](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-relogin-0.trace.jsonl), [relogin1](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-relogin-1.trace.jsonl), [new-character guard](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-guard-newCharacter.trace.jsonl), [start-game guard](public/1792977859487-2ff0ea0f-guard-startGame.trace.jsonl). These already-audited public traces were opaque-hashed once for the prerequisite; the copier only copies and hashes bytes.\n- [Current preparation](preparation/template-prepared-v2.json), [actual binding derivation](preparation/actual-K-binding-derivation-v2.json), [Root final launcher binding](preparation/launcher-final-binding-v1.json), [prepared-source review](review/scout-selection-diagnostics-full16-independent-review-v2.json), [actual facts review](review/scout-selection-diagnostics-full16-actual-independent-facts-v1.json). The preparation README is preserved as its actual-bound, not-yet-executed history.\n- [Actual prerequisite](full16-actual-prerequisite-v1.json), [Root OS cleanup](execution/scout-selection-diagnostics-full16-root-independent-cleanup-v1.json), [Node232 receipt](source/root-full-driver-receipt-v1.json), [current freeze](source/capacity-scout-selection-diagnostics-driver-frozen-v1.json), [actual readonly runtime guard](source/runtime/scout-selection-diagnostics-runtime-readonly-guard-stdout-v1.log), [Node diagnostic validation](../capacity-scout-selection-diagnostics-driver-v1/README.md).\n\nOnly the explicit closed public/source/evidence whitelist is copied. Private stores, credentials, binary payloads, recordings, capacity raw and future Probe20 results are excluded. Capacity/P0 remain false and P2 remains frozen.\n"
